# systemd presets for policy mode KIOSK.
#
# A preset is a declaration, not an enforcement. apply-policy runs the real enable/disable/mask for
# every line below. See 85-auros-managed.preset.
#
# getty is disabled here and MASKED by apply-policy. Ctrl+Alt+F2 on a kiosk machine must not produce a
# login prompt: the whole claim of the mode is that there is one application and no way past it, and a
# text console is a way past it for anyone holding any set of credentials.
#
# What that costs, recorded rather than discovered: a kiosk machine with a broken kiosk service has no
# local console to fix it from. Recovery is the GRUB path or a reimage. See policy/README.md,
# "what kiosk costs you".
enable auros-kiosk.service
enable bootc-fetch-apply-updates.timer
disable getty@.service
disable serial-getty@.service
disable debug-shell.service
disable sddm.service
disable gdm.service
disable lightdm.service
disable display-manager.service
